#: desc: A comment continued with a backslash (a doc too) is joined with the next line
-v COLOR=0 test/fixtures/Makefile.backslash-comments
#: stdout
-----------------------
Available targets:
-----------------------
t-tab                 A doc indented with a tab (outside a rule) continued
t-space-tab           A doc indented with a space and a tab continued
t-joined              A doc continued on the next line
t-blanks              A doc continued with blanks around the backslash-newline
t-two-backslashes     A doc that ends with two backslashes (not continued) \\
t-three-backslashes   A doc that ends with three backslashes (continued) \\ on the next line
t-after-target        A continued doc swallows the next line, a target t-swallowed:
t-after-variable      A continued doc swallows the next line, a variable V_SWALLOWED := 1 ## part of the doc above
t-plain-comment       A doc kept above a continued plain comment
 A section continued
t-section             A doc below the section
t-doc-doc             A doc ## continued with a doc line
-----------------------
